{
  "uid": "grots-http-semconv",
  "title": "Grot's Pizzeria: HTTP semantic conventions",
  "description": "HTTP server and client telemetry (metrics, logs and traces) for every application in Grot's Pizzeria, with notes on what the semantic conventions say about what is shown: open \"How to read this dashboard\".",
  "tags": [
    "grots-pizzeria",
    "opentelemetry",
    "semantic-conventions"
  ],
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "version": 1,
  "editable": true,
  "graphTooltip": 1,
  "refresh": "auto",
  "time": {
    "from": "now-30m",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "timepicker": {},
  "templating": {
    "list": [
      {
        "name": "service",
        "label": "Application",
        "type": "query",
        "datasource": {
          "type": "prometheus",
          "uid": "prometheus"
        },
        "query": {
          "query": "label_values({__name__=~\"http_server_request_duration_seconds_count|http_client_request_duration_seconds_count\"}, service_name)",
          "refId": "service"
        },
        "definition": "label_values({__name__=~\"http_server_request_duration_seconds_count|http_client_request_duration_seconds_count\"}, service_name)",
        "refresh": 2,
        "sort": 1,
        "multi": true,
        "includeAll": true,
        "allValue": ".+",
        "current": {
          "selected": true,
          "text": [
            "All"
          ],
          "value": [
            "$__all"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "search",
        "label": "Log search",
        "type": "textbox",
        "query": "",
        "current": {
          "text": "",
          "value": ""
        },
        "options": [
          {
            "selected": true,
            "text": "",
            "value": ""
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "annotations": {
    "list": [
      {
        "builtIn": 1,
        "datasource": {
          "type": "grafana",
          "uid": "-- Grafana --"
        },
        "enable": true,
        "hide": true,
        "iconColor": "rgba(0, 211, 255, 1)",
        "name": "Annotations & Alerts",
        "type": "dashboard"
      }
    ]
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 101,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "How to read this dashboard",
      "collapsed": true,
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 1
      },
      "panels": [
        {
          "id": 100,
          "type": "text",
          "title": "How to read this dashboard",
          "gridPos": {
            "x": 0,
            "y": 1,
            "w": 24,
            "h": 11
          },
          "options": {
            "mode": "markdown",
            "content": "**Durations are in seconds.** `http.server.request.duration` and `http.client.request.duration` are histograms in seconds. Grafana writes the unit that suits the value.\n\n**Routes are templates, not URLs.** `http.route` is the route that matched (`/api/orders/{id}`), so there is a series for each route and not for each order. The URL that was asked for is on the spans (`url.path`).\n\n**Only a 5xx is a server error.** The HTTP 5xx rate counts the application failing. A 4xx is the caller's mistake or a correct refusal (a declined payment is a 402), and is not an error for the server that sent it, but it is one for the client that received it: that is why the outbound panels show it and the inbound one does not."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "HTTP server (http.server.request.duration)",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 1
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Requests / s",
      "description": "Inbound HTTP requests per second across the selected applications. With All selected this counts service hops, not orders: one order is a request to the BFF and then one each to orders, menu, checkout and delivery, plus the UI polling the tracking. Health checks are not counted: no application records them.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 2,
        "w": 6,
        "h": 4
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum(rate(http_server_request_duration_seconds_count{service_name=~\"$service\"}[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "",
          "refId": "A",
          "range": false,
          "instant": true
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "reqps",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          },
          "decimals": 2
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "textMode": "auto"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "HTTP 5xx rate",
      "description": "The share of inbound requests answered with a 5xx status: the application failed. It is not every kind of error. A 4xx is the caller's mistake or a correct refusal, such as the 402 for a declined payment or the 404 for someone else's order, and is not counted, which is also how the semantic conventions treat server spans (only a 5xx makes one an error). See \"Responses by status code\" for the others. Shows 0% once there has been traffic and no failures, and no data until there has been any traffic at all.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 6,
        "y": 2,
        "w": 6,
        "h": 4
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "(sum(rate(http_server_request_duration_seconds_count{service_name=~\"$service\", http_response_status_code=~\"5..\"}[$__rate_interval])) or vector(0)) / sum(rate(http_server_request_duration_seconds_count{service_name=~\"$service\"}[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "",
          "refId": "A",
          "range": false,
          "instant": true
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "orange",
                "value": 0.01
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 0.05
              }
            ]
          },
          "decimals": 2
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "textMode": "auto"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "p95 latency",
      "description": "The 95th percentile of http.server.request.duration: 95% of requests were answered at least this quickly. The metric is in seconds. A percentile is worked out from the histogram's buckets, so it needs enough requests in the time range to mean anything: with a handful it is only as good as the bucket it falls in. Generate some traffic with scripts/generate-traffic.ps1.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 12,
        "y": 2,
        "w": 6,
        "h": 4
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le) (rate(http_server_request_duration_seconds_bucket{service_name=~\"$service\"}[$__rate_interval])))",
          "legendFormat": "",
          "refId": "A",
          "range": false,
          "instant": true
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "orange",
                "value": 0.5
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          "decimals": 3
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "textMode": "auto"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Applications reporting",
      "description": "Applications that served at least one request in the selected time range.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 18,
        "y": 2,
        "w": 6,
        "h": 4
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "count(count by (service_name) (last_over_time(http_server_request_duration_seconds_count{service_name=~\"$service\"}[$__range])))",
          "legendFormat": "",
          "refId": "A",
          "range": false,
          "instant": true
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "none",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          },
          "decimals": 0
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "textMode": "auto"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Requests by application, method and route",
      "description": "rate(http.server.request.duration) by service.name, http.request.method and http.route. The route is the template that matched, such as /api/orders/{id}, and not the URL that was requested, such as /api/orders/ord_1a2b3c4d5e6f. The URL is on the spans, as url.path.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 6,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 9
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (service_name, http_request_method, http_route) (rate(http_server_request_duration_seconds_count{service_name=~\"$service\"}[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{service_name}} {{http_request_method}} {{http_route}}",
          "refId": "A",
          "range": true
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "reqps",
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 15,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "stacking": {
              "mode": "none"
            }
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "calcs": [
            "mean",
            "max"
          ]
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Latency percentiles by application",
      "description": "p50 / p95 / p99 of http.server.request.duration, in seconds. The higher the percentile, the more requests it needs to be worked out from: p99 is the slowest 1 in 100, so with fewer than 100 requests it is mostly one request. Generate some traffic (scripts/generate-traffic.ps1) to see the lines settle.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 12,
        "y": 6,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 9
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.5, sum by (le, service_name) (rate(http_server_request_duration_seconds_bucket{service_name=~\"$service\"}[$__rate_interval])))",
          "legendFormat": "p50 {{service_name}}",
          "refId": "A",
          "range": true
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
